# Tenor Labs (Morpho Midnight) - Dust Fill Collateral Rounding Exploit

## Severity: High (Unsubmitted due to $250 deposit requirement)

## Summary
The `CollateralTransferLib.transferCollaterals` function in Tenor Labs uses `mulDivDown` to calculate pro-rata collateral transfers. If a borrower has accrued interest (making debt slightly larger than collateral), a tiny "dust fill" (e.g., 1 wei) causes the calculated collateral to transfer to round down to `0`. This leaves the target position with unbacked debt and an artificially inflated LTV.

## Proof of Concept
The included Foundry test (`DustFillExploit.t.sol`) proves this vulnerability locally. 

## How to run:
1. `forge install`
2. `forge test --match-contract DustFillExploit -vvv`

